Process to create a new action (ideally to make it slightly clearer for others and myself cause I've messed up every single step on here)

1. Make the new action class - inheriting from "Progress_Action" or "Action"
    This will have most of the functionality:
        Start() - runs at the start of the action (need to super.start() for progress_action to create progress_bar)
            returns True for successful start; false for some sort of error (ie: structure or tile undefined)
        Update() - runs every frame while action is running
        End(interrupted) - runs at the end of the action - param: interrupted -- bool -- if the action was interrupted (ie: moving away while building)
            returns True if action was successful; false if not (ie: was interrupted) 
        set_location() and set_action_item() ran when action is scheduled (in this order)
            super() -> sets location of cursor (tile your interacting with) 
                    -> action_item varies (ie: structure you're building or source you're mining from)
                        default is item currently selected (in ui)
2. In the player class (or specific entity class that does the action)
    1. add the action to the entity_actions dictionary
    2. add the action to the update_animations function 
        *Make sure to handle both the start of the action and interrupt at the bottom
3. Add the scheduling of the action to mouse_commands
    1. Chose specific mouse button to signal start of action (make sure it doesnt conflict with other actions/does different action depending on situation)
    2. Make specific method that checks all the special cases (like building on top of something else or deconstructing a source without a miner)
    3. set the self.action_trigger to the name of the action
    4. run set_location and set_action_item depending on what the functionality of those functions is
4. Add in all the necessary assets 
    1. Player animation for the action
    2. Progress bar stuffs (for progress action)
5. Figure out what I forgot on this list when it doesnt work :)
    